B.ccR=new A.ce("Wrap the dashcn subtree in its Theme so tokens resolve even when the root app is Material-owned:",null,null)
B.ccS=new A.ce("Every component resolves its style through four legs, from highest to lowest priority: a widget argument, the nearest ComponentTheme in the tree, the app overrides registered at the root, then the token-derived defaults.",null,null)
B.ccT=new A.ce("Guideline thresholds: tap-target checks use the mobile tap-target guideline (44/48 px). They are informational for desktop-sized controls (36 px buttons and rows) and are never hidden when they fail.",null,null)
B.ccU=new A.ce("Every component ships twice from the same source: as the published dashcn package and as copyable files the CLI installs into your app. Both render the same widgets from the same theme tokens; they differ only in who owns the bytes.",null,null)
B.ccV=new A.ce("Use the components two ways, from the same source: depend on the published package and update via semver, or copy the sources into your project and own them. Pick a tab \u2014 the steps below walk the own-the-code flow.",null,null)
B.ccW=new A.ce("After installation, your project has the registry layer core (foundation + theme) and the components you added. Run the app to see the components in action.",null,null)
B.ccX=new A.ce("With the prefix, both sets stay usable in one build method: Material owns the scaffold, dashcn owns the action.",null,null)
B.ccY=new A.ce("Choose the package when you want semver updates and lean imports. Choose own-the-code when you want to read, edit and commit every line.",null,null)
B.ccZ=new A.ce("Test environment timing: frame times are measured with a stopwatch around pumped frames in the test VM. They compare components relatively; they never predict device frame rates.",null,null)
B.cd_=new A.ce("Right-to-left pumps the preview under Right-to-left direction and checks that it renders with no exception or overflow. Mirroring compares the first Text x in Left-to-right versus Right-to-left: a shift means directional content, equal positions mean a symmetric layout, and no text means not applicable.",null,null)
B.cd0=new A.ce("AnimatedTheme animates ThemeData changes over the duration and curve you pass. Colours tween; layout does not, so a preset or mode switch never reflows the page.",null,null)
B.cd1=new A.ce("Every component in this kit is copied into your app, so the source is yours to read, edit and extend. The registry defines each component once: its widget file, its style file, its theme overrides and a generated manifest the CLI installs from.",null,null)
B.cd2=new A.ce("Two optional mode-independent tokens make floating surfaces frosted: surfaceOpacity (0..1) multiplies every surface fill, and surfaceBlur (logical px) blurs the backdrop behind it. Cards, dialogs, popovers, menus, tooltips, toasts, sheets, the navigation bar and the scaffold app bar all read them, so one preset change frosts the whole app. The defaults stay opaque (no extra layer), and a component theme value wins over the global when both are set.",null,null)
B.cd3=new A.ce("Test font: the harness pumps previews under the default theme fallback with the test font, so muted text near 4.35 to 4.43 contrast can fail the 4.5 threshold without failing on device fonts.",null,null)
B.cd4=new A.ce("The app leg is the user-owned <name>_theme.dart file the CLI writes next to each component. CLI updates never overwrite it, so your overrides survive an upgrade.",null,null)
B.cd5=new A.ce("radius is the base radius factor: the unitless rem number a preset stores. The component radius steps derive from it, so a single value updates every rounded surface.",null,null)
B.cd6=new A.ce("A toggle stores an explicit mode. Once the user chooses, stop following the platform and persist the choice so the next visit opens in the same mode.",null,null)
B.cd7=new A.ce("Reduced motion collapses everything: when the platform reports MediaQuery.disableAnimations, or the Theme Studio Motion row switches motion.enabled off, every animation resolves to zero duration and its end value, with no tickers or timers running.",null,null)
B.cd9=new A.ce("Every component animation resolves through the motion tokens, read as Theme.of(context).motion. Durations stay in the subtle band \u2014 instant 100 ms, fast 150 ms, base 200 ms, slow 300 ms \u2014 and curves stay restrained, except the spring overshoot used for press-release and pop-in effects. Motion is transform and opacity only, so it never changes layout or a final state.",null,null)
B.cda=new A.ce("On phones dashcn grows desktop-density controls with transparent hit padding (iOS 44, Android 48) without changing the painted visuals. Dense rows and joined groups can opt out per app with ThemeData(touchTargets: TouchTargets.shrinkWrap).",null,null)
B.cdb=new A.ce("Try them on the Themes page, or read the Theming page to see how a preset maps onto the token names.",null,null)
B.cdc=new A.ce("Each component page shows a trust scorecard: accessibility, right-to-left, frame build time and tests. The numbers come from a generated harness run over the component previews; a missing measurement is shown as \u201cNot measured\u201d, never as a pass.",null,null)
B.cdd=new A.ce("Tokens come in semantic background/foreground pairs. The base token controls the surface colour and the -foreground token controls the text and icons that sit on that surface, so a component never hard-codes a contrast colour.",null,null)
B.cde=new A.ce("Tests counts registry test cases tagged to the component (file prefix or folder under test/registry/components, plus tags component:<id>). Pass reflects the scorecard harness run at generation time, not the registry suite result.",null,null)
B.c3m=new A.bQ("Own-the-code apps stay on the package path too: run ",null,null,B.Q,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.ccP=new A.ip("dashcn eject button",null)
B.cfl=new A.ez(B.ccP,B.fw,null,null)
B.c2I=new A.bQ(" later to turn a package import into owned sources.",null,null,B.Q,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
B.bz6=s([B.c3m,B.cfl,B.c2I],t.VO)
B.cdf=new A.ce("",B.bz6,null)
B.cdg=new A.ce("Exemptions: a check with a documented reason (a decorative divider excluded from semantics, a disabled row WCAG exempts from contrast, a sampling artefact) renders as \u201cExempt\u201d with its reason and never counts as a failure.",null,null)
B.cdh=new A.ce("Accessibility checks the preview with the framework guidelines: text contrast (4.5 minimum), labeled tap targets, Android tap targets (48 by 48) and iOS tap targets (44 by 44), plus whether any semantics label, value, hint or tooltip is present.",null,null)
B.cdi=new A.ce("The CLI manages the registry lifecycle: install the layer core, add components with their dependency closure, update from upstream, and validate the install. All commands are snapshot-derived from the CLI help text.",null,null)
B.cdj=new A.ce("Per-component imports keep package-mode builds lean; only the components you import are compiled in.",null,null)
B.cdk=new A.ce("One root owns the app: use DashcnApp for a full dashcn app (localizations, theme mode and navigation come from the kit) and MaterialApp when Material owns the shell with dashcn islands inside. Never nest one root inside the other.",null,null)
B.cdm=new A.ce("The kit generator runs a generated harness test with the JSON reporter, collects one SCORECARD record per component, counts tests with the analyzer, and writes lib/src/manifests/scorecards.json. The docs generator then emits lib/generated/docs_scorecards.dart from that manifest.",null,null)
B.cdn=new A.ce("Every preset defines a light and a dark token set. Dark mode is not a filter over the light theme: it is a second set of the same tokens, so components read one code path in both modes.",null,null)
B.cdo=new A.ce("Every measured component with its overall badge. Sort by failures to surface the components with the most failing checks.",null,null)
B.cdp=new A.ce("Build your theme from tokens. Every colour, radius, font and shadow a component reads comes from the active ThemeData, so a preset switch re-themes the whole app without touching component code.",null,null)
B.cdq=new A.ce("Theme, ThemeData, Card, Chip, Dialog, Slider, Switch, Checkbox, Tooltip, showDialog and showMenu exist in both libraries. Import one side with a prefix or hide the names you do not use:",null,null)
B.cdr=new A.ce("dashcn.lock (v2) records the registry reference, the install root, the theme selection and \u2014 per component \u2014 whether it is a package dependency or owned sources. .dashcn/config.json holds the install path and registry source. Commit both.",null,null)
B.cds=new A.ce("dashcn is widgets-only: it never imports Material, and a pure dashcn app never needs it. Inside an existing Material app the components still work \u2014 only a few names collide.",null,null)
B.cdt=new A.ce("Frame build time pumps 120 frames of 16 ms and reports the p50 and p90 build times in milliseconds. It is labelled \u201cFrame build time \u2014 test environment (relative)\u201d: relative numbers for comparing components, not device performance.",null,null)
B.cdu=new A.ce("There is exactly one implementation per component. No variant wrappers, no per-style subclasses and no Material widgets under the hood; the components are built from the kit primitives and the active theme tokens.",null,null)
B.cdv=new A.ce("Can\u2019t find what you need? Every component installs as editable source, so a missing piece can start from the closest match and grow with your app.",null,null)
